# The Docker build context is the repo root (see apps/api.saroh.in/Dockerfile).
# Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image, irrelevant to the api, or
# a secret that must never be baked into a layer.

# Never. A COPY would put these in an image layer that survives every later
# deletion, and the CI cache export (mode=max) pushes intermediate layers to
# the registry.
#
# The `**/` forms are NOT redundant. A bare `.env` matches ONLY the context
# root, so without these, every one of these real secret files would enter the
# build context:
#     apps/api.saroh.in/.env      apps/admin.saroh.in/.env
#     apps/accounts.saroh.in/.env apps/app.saroh.in/.env
#     apps/saroh.in/.env          apps/saroh.app/.env
#     packages/database/.env
# `turbo prune` happens to drop gitignored files from its output, so the FINAL
# image was clean — but the pruner stage still held them, and that stage is
# exported by `cache-to: mode=max`.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Rebuilt in the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated by `turbo run build`.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Caches
.turbo
**/.turbo
.eslintcache
coverage
**/coverage

# VCS + tooling noise
.git
.github
.husky
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Agent/worktree scratch
.claude
.agents
.cursor
.impeccable
.worktrees

# Not needed to build or run the api
docs
internal-decision-docs
scripts
infra
*.md
